# API Contract Rules

Public specifications live under `packages/openapi/`:

- Root aggregate: `packages/openapi/openapi.yaml`
- Service specs: `identity-service.yaml`, `company-service.yaml`, `transport-order-service.yaml`, `rfx-service.yaml`, `shipment-service.yaml`, `document-service.yaml`, `billing-register-service.yaml`
- Shared schemas: `packages/openapi/schemas/`

When a public API contract changes:

- Update OpenAPI alongside implementation.
- Keep implementation and specification aligned; avoid undocumented endpoints.
- Avoid silent response-shape or status-code changes.
- Maintain backwards compatibility by default; explicitly report breaking changes.
- Run `make openapi-validate` or `make openapi-check` when contract files change.
- Gateway and downstream contract changes require coordinated verification.

Do not rewrite API contracts without a diagnostic report and explicit task authorization.
